+ * EVERY FRAME, so every frame rendered with no depth buffer at all. The colour texture is
+ * m_width * m_scale rounded down; the depth texture was created before its colour buffer existed
+ * and took the window width instead. One pixel apart, and the GLES branch above tests ==.
+ *
+ * ⚠ AND IT IS NOT THIS PORT'S DRIVER. The same run on the host's native radeonsi - no zink, no
+ * RADV-on-Liverpool, no thunks of ours - drops just as often. Any GLES3 machine running this core
+ * with framebuffer emulation has it; desktop GL does not, because the branch below it tolerates a
+ * larger depth texture and a one-pixel difference in m_width, and that is exactly what is used
+ * here. With it, the drops go to zero and Mesa reports no error it was not already reporting.
+ *
+ * Set from /data/retroarch-gliden64; `depthWidthLoose=0` puts upstream's test back. */
+extern "C" int orbis_gliden64_depth_width_loose;
 #endif
 
